{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each valve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, when open, releases water into a tank at its own constant rate. With all three valves open, the tank fills in 1 hour, with only valves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> open it takes 1.5 hours, and with only valves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> open it takes 2 hours. The number of hours required with only valves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> open is \n</p><p>\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a800666d570b467ecf27543978c042e35dbcc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1.1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1.15\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1.2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 1.25\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"446\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the rate of water flowing through valve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the rate of water flowing through valve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and the rate of water flowing through valve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let the volume of the tank be 1 liter, and let the units for the rates be liters per hour.  With this information, we can write three equations.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331b6d5079993775c873b8292f01213bf0c6f2ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a+b+c} = 1\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e576a6be4e7196e199aaad515b265830a1e3ef6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a+c} = \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/dddc52b632fffdfb006bb99eccd06dd2a400aa99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{b+c} = 2\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" />\nManipulate each equation to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa5ee6303703937c528de293e4960d435904e67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = a+b+c\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb64e81b2c6b44c65ab084b92ec4052e07be675.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{3} = a+c\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/23042f3ff9302c9bbca0df9174d20604d62ee5e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} = b+c\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24eefa9b64d7a323655270dab02092bc01915270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"21\" />, and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abceee14da6aec8d67139507170529aba9ecab93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\tfrac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"44\" height=\"23\" />.  The number of hours to fill the tub with only valves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf8dbf677848aa9dc17cd97fad4fb4da3985fc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{6}{5} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1.2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"178\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSM